# XSH fork(), _Fork()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Children report by exit status; the parent judges.

assertion  XSH.fork.001
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fork.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       fork() creates a process: it returns 0 in the child and the
           child's process ID (positive) in the parent, and both carry
           on from the call.
test       t/001-returns.c

assertion  XSH.fork.002
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       The child has a process ID of its own, different from the
           parent's, and its parent process ID is the parent's process
           ID.
test       t/002-ids.c

assertion  XSH.fork.003
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       The child's process ID is not the ID of any active process
           group: right after fork() there is no process group with that
           ID.
test       t/003-not-a-group.c

assertion  XSH.fork.004
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       The child has copies of the parent's descriptors, each
           referring to the same open file description: an lseek() in
           the child moves the parent's offset.
test       t/004-descriptors.c

assertion  XSH.fork.005
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A descriptor with FD_CLOFORK set is not in the child; one
           without it is.
note       Blocked when XBD.fcntl.h.002 (FD_CLOFORK) fails.
uses       XBD.fcntl.h.002
test       t/005-clofork.c

assertion  XSH.fork.006
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       The child has its own copy of the parent's open directory
           streams: readdir() works on a stream the parent opened.
test       t/006-dirstream.c

assertion  XSH.fork.007
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       In the child, times() starts again: tms_cutime and tms_cstime
           are 0, and tms_utime is below the CPU time the parent had
           used.
note       The parent first uses about 0.3 s of CPU and reaps a child
           that did too.
test       t/007-times.c

assertion  XSH.fork.008
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       A pending alarm() in the parent is cancelled in the child:
           alarm(0) there returns 0.
test       t/008-alarm.c

assertion  XSH.fork.009
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       The child starts with no pending signals, even when a signal
           is pending in the parent.
test       t/009-pending.c

assertion  XSH.fork.010
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       A MAP_PRIVATE mapping is kept in the child with the parent's
           data from before fork(); after fork(), each process's changes
           to it are visible only to itself.
nomutant   not planted yet: needs a fault in mmap() or a copy-on-write
           emulation
test       t/010-map-private.c

assertion  XSH.fork.011
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       A MAP_SHARED mapping is kept in the child: a change the child
           makes is seen by the parent.
nomutant   not planted yet: needs a fault in mmap()
test       t/011-map-shared.c

assertion  XSH.fork.012
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       Per-process timers made with timer_create() are not
           inherited: a timer armed in the parent before fork() does not
           signal the child, while it does signal the parent.
test       t/012-timer.c

assertion  XSH.fork.013
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       The child of a multi-threaded process has only the thread
           that called fork(): another parent thread that keeps counting
           does not run in the child.
nomutant   extra threads in the child cannot be planted from a preload
           library
test       t/013-single-thread.c

assertion  XSH.fork.014
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       TSH
since      2001
says       TSH: a process-shared mutex held by the parent is not held by
           the child: unlocking that error-checking mutex in the child
           fails with EPERM.
nomutant   not planted yet: needs a fault in pthread_mutex_unlock()
note       The fork() page does not shade this item TSH, but only TSH
           makes a lock process-shared: see SI-7.
test       t/014-pshared-mutex.c

assertion  XSH.fork.015
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       CPT
since      2001
says       CPT: the child's CPU-time clock starts at zero: just after
           fork() it reads less than the CPU time the parent had used.
note       The parent first uses about 0.3 s of CPU.
test       t/015-cputime.c

assertion  XSH.fork.016
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       A named semaphore open in the parent is open in the child:
           the child's sem_post() releases the parent's sem_wait().
nomutant   not planted yet: needs a fault in sem_post()
test       t/016-semaphore.c

assertion  XSH.fork.017
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       Other process attributes are the same in the child: the
           umask, the working directory, the signal mask, ignored
           signals, the environment, RLIMIT_NOFILE, the process group
           and the session.
test       t/017-same-state.c

assertion  XSH.fork.018
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION/_Fork
class      required
since      2024
says       _Fork() creates a child as fork() does but runs none of the
           handlers registered with pthread_atfork() (prepare, parent or
           child), all of which fork() runs.
note       _Fork() is new in Issue 8; a library that does not declare it
           makes the test UNINITIATED (build failure).
test       t/018-_Fork.c

assertion  XSH.fork.019
anchor     functions/fork.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       After fork() parent and child run independently, before either
           ends: they exchange 100 messages over pipes, each waiting for
           the other.
test       t/019-independent.c

